      "bhavartha": "Earth, water, fire, wind and space, the five elements of the world: He is none of them. Tiredness and sleep do not belong to Him, nor heat and cold; He has no place and no dress, and no form at all. And still the poet praises Him as the Trimūrti, the One who has three forms."
    },
